// Pull request author: stuartjash
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Hidden Executable Run From Shared
// Sigma ID: d6db13e8-542c-4683-97bf-f9e6dc3d966d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Stuart Ashenbrenner
// Date: 2026-09-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036.005
// Description: Detects the execution of a hidden file (name starting with a dot) located in the /Users/Shared
//   directory. Masquerading an executable as a dot-file in a shared location is a technique observed
//   in the BlueNoroff macOS intrusion set (TA444) and reduces its visibility in a casual listing.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate scripts or installers that hide files in /Users/Shared
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/inside-bluenoroff-web3-intrusion-analysis
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ae9128c7ebd868a0d436fa9897f05d275ef26207/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_hidden_exec_shared.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath matches regex "^/Users/Shared/\\.[a-zA-Z0-9._-]{1,255}$"
